INSERT INTO `exam_questions` VALUES ('afcat-1','IAF command locations and aircraft origins (Rafale, Sukhoi, Tejas, Apache) are guaranteed AFCAT questions.',2,'Easy','The Maintenance Command of the Indian Air Force is headquartered at Vayusena Nagar in Nagpur, Maharashtra.','[\"New Delhi\",\"Prayagraj (Allahabad)\",\"Nagpur\",\"Shillong\"]','Where is the permanent headquarters of the Maintenance Command of the Indian Air Force located?','Military Aptitude & Static GK','Indian Air Force Commands','AI Predicted 2026','afcat-exam'),('agni-1','Military awards and army rank equivalents are standard Agniveer GK questions.',1,'Easy','Param Vir Chakra (PVC) is India\'s highest military decoration awarded for displaying supreme acts of valour during wartime.','[\"Ashoka Chakra\",\"Param Vir Chakra\",\"Maha Vir Chakra\",\"Shaurya Chakra\"]','Which of the following is the highest wartime gallantry military decoration awarded by the Republic of India for conspicuous bravery in the presence of the enemy?','General Knowledge & Military','Gallantry Awards','2024','agniveer-exam'),('alp-1','Engineering drawing tools and dimensions are mandatory questions for RRB ALP CBT 2.',2,'Medium','Standard BIS drawing boards: B0 is 1500x1000, B1 is 1000x700, B2 is 700x500x15mm, and B3 is 500x350x15mm.','[\"1500 x 1000 x 25\",\"1000 x 700 x 25\",\"700 x 500 x 15\",\"500 x 350 x 15\"]','As per standard BIS drawing board specifications, what are the exact dimensions (in mm) of a standard B2 designated drawing board?','Basic Science & Engineering Drawing','Engineering Drawing Standards','2024','rrb-alp'),('bank-po-1','Reverse syllogisms and \"Only a few\" condition logic are tested in every banking Prelims.',0,'Hard','\"Only a few\" means some are and some definitely are not. Since all Funds are Markets and no Market is a Loss, any Bank that is a Fund is also a Market, so it cannot be a Loss. Thus, some Banks (which are Funds) are definitely not Losses (Conclusion I follows). Conclusion II is false because \"only a few\" explicitly prevents all Banks from becoming Funds.','[\"Only conclusion I follows\",\"Only conclusion II follows\",\"Both I and II follow\",\"Neither I nor II follows\"]','Statements:\nOnly a few Banks are Funds.\nAll Funds are Markets.\nNo Market is a Loss.\nConclusions:\nI. Some Banks are definitely not Losses.\nII. All Banks being Funds is a possibility.','Reasoning Ability','Syllogism (Only a few)','AI Predicted 2026','ibps-po'),('bank-po-2','Monetary policy instruments (Repo, CRR, OMO, MSF) are standard Banking Awareness questions.',1,'Medium','Selling government securities means banks pay money to the RBI to purchase those bonds, draining/absorbing surplus cash liquidity from the commercial banking system.','[\"Liquidity in the banking system increases\",\"Liquidity in the banking system is absorbed / decreases\",\"Repo rate automatically reduces to 0%\",\"Foreign exchange reserves immediately double\"]','When the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) conducts Open Market Operations (OMOs) by selling government securities in the secondary market, what is the direct impact on liquidity?','Banking & Financial Awareness','Monetary Policy Tools','2024','ibps-po'),('bits-1','Verbal analogies and logical speed math are the defining differentiators for BITSAT aspirants.',1,'Medium','Cacophony and Harmony are antonyms (discordant noise vs. beautiful balance). Tempestuous (stormy/turbulent) and Serene (calm/peaceful) exhibit the exact same antonymous relationship.','[\"Belligerent : Hostile\",\"Tempestuous : Serene\",\"Garrulous : Talkative\",\"Lethargic : Sluggish\"]','Select the pair that best expresses a similar relationship to: \"CACOPHONY : HARMONY\"','English Proficiency','Verbal Analogies','AI Predicted 2026','bitsat-exam'),('capf-1','Indigenized defence technology and bilateral joint military ventures are guaranteed questions in CAPF and CDS.',1,'Medium','Barak-8 (Medium Range Surface to Air Missile - MRSAM) is an Indo-Israeli surface-to-air missile designed to defend against any type of airborne threat.','[\"Akash\",\"Barak-8 (MRSAM)\",\"Prithvi Air Defence (PAD)\",\"S-400 Triumf\"]','Which of the following air defence missile systems is jointly developed by India\'s DRDO and Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI)?','General Science & Defence','Defence Technology & Missiles','AI Predicted 2026','upsc-capf'),('capf-2','Tribunals and judicial hierarchies are highly recurring CAPF Polity topics.',2,'Medium','Under the Armed Forces Tribunal Act 2007, an appeal against the final order or judgment of the Tribunal lies directly before the Supreme Court of India.','[\"High Court of the respective jurisdiction\",\"President of India\",\"Supreme Court of India\",\"Chief of Defence Staff\"]','Appeals against final orders or judgments of the Armed Forces Tribunal (AFT) lie directly before:','Polity & Governance','Armed Forces Tribunal','2024','upsc-capf'),('cat-1','Logarithm and quadratic progression questions consistently feature in CAT QA with 2-3 questions per slot.',0,'Medium','Using log base change: log_4(x) = (1/2)log_2(x) and log_16(x) = (1/4)log_2(x). Sum = log_2(x) * [1 + 1/2 + 1/4] = (7/4) log_2(x) = 21/4. Therefore, log_2(x) = 3, which implies x = 2^3 = 8.','[\"8\",\"16\",\"32\",\"64\"]','If log_2(x) + log_4(x) + log_16(x) = 21/4, what is the exact value of x?','Quantitative Aptitude','Algebra & Progressions','AI Predicted 2026','cat-mba'),('cat-2','Euler totient theorem and modular arithmetic power cycles are standard CAT QA patterns.',0,'Medium','Note that 7^3 = 343. 343 = 1 mod 342. 7^84 = (7^3)^28 = (343)^28 = (1)^28 = 1 mod 342.','[\"1\",\"7\",\"49\",\"341\"]','What is the remainder when 7^84 is divided by 342?','Quantitative Aptitude','Number System','2024','cat-mba'),('cds-1','Equilateral triangle properties inside circle tangents appear in almost every single CDS exam cycle.',2,'Easy','Tangents drawn from an external point are equal in length, so PA = PB. In triangle PAB, since PA = PB, angle PAB = angle PBA. With angle APB = 60°, triangle PAB becomes an equilateral triangle. Hence, chord AB = PA = 10 cm.','[\"5 cm\",\"10 * sqrt(3) cm\",\"10 cm\",\"5 * sqrt(3) cm\"]','From an external point P, two tangents PA and PB are drawn to a circle with centre O. If angle APB = 60° and length PA = 10 cm, what is the length of the chord AB?','Elementary Mathematics','Geometry - Circles & Tangents','AI Predicted 2026','upsc-cds'),('chsl-1','Multiplication by consecutive numbers is the most common SSC number series pattern.',2,'Medium','The underlying logic is N : (N^2 - N). For 14: 14^2 - 14 = 196 - 14 = 182? Wait, let\'s check 14 * 15 = 210. So N : N * (N + 1). For 16: 16 * 17 = 272.','[\"240\",\"256\",\"272\",\"288\"]','In a certain logic, 14 : 210 :: 16 : ?','General Intelligence & Reasoning','Number Series & Analogies','AI Predicted 2026','ssc-chsl'),('cisf-1','Standard statutory date question. Mandatory for all departmental aspirants.',1,'Easy','CISF was established in 1969 under the CISF Act of Parliament to provide integrated security cover to public sector undertakings.','[\"1965\",\"1969\",\"1973\",\"1984\"]','The Central Industrial Security Force (CISF) was enacted under an Act of Parliament in which year?','Professional Security Skills & Laws','CISF Act','2024','upsc-cisf'),('clat-1','Constitutional landmark judgments and recent Supreme Court verdicts represent 35+ marks in CLAT legal reasoning passages.',1,'Medium','In the historic Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973) judgment, a 13-judge constitutional bench ruled by a 7-6 majority that Article 368 does not enable Parliament to alter the basic structure or framework of the Constitution.','[\"Golaknath Case (1967)\",\"Kesavananda Bharati Case (1973)\",\"Minerva Mills Case (1980)\",\"S.R. Bommai Case (1994)\"]','The landmark constitutional principle known as the \"Basic Structure Doctrine\", which establishes that Parliament cannot alter the fundamental architecture of the Constitution under Article 368, was promulgated by the Supreme Court in:','Legal Reasoning & Constitutional Principles','Basic Structure Doctrine','AI Predicted 2026','clat-law'),('clerk-1','Simplification and approximation questions represent 10-15 direct marks in banking clerical preliminary tests.',1,'Easy','35% of 600 = 210. Equation: 210 + (x/100)*500 = 360. 5x = 360 - 210 = 150. x = 30.','[\"25\",\"30\",\"35\",\"40\"]','What exact value will come in place of the question mark (?):\n35% of 600 + ? % of 500 = 360','Quantitative Aptitude','Rapid Simplification','AI Predicted 2026','ibps-clerk'),('cms-1','Tropical vector-borne diseases and diagnostic markers are standard 5-mark blocks in CMS Paper 1.',1,'Easy','The classic triad of fever, retro-orbital pain, severe myalgia (\"break-bone fever\"), thrombocytopenia, and positive NS1 antigen is highly specific for Dengue fever.','[\"Typhoid Fever\",\"Dengue Fever\",\"Malaria (P. falciparum)\",\"Leptospirosis\"]','A 35-year-old patient presents with high fever, severe retro-orbital headache, myalgia, and a maculopapular rash. Lab investigations reveal platelet count of 45,000/mcL and positive NS1 antigen. What is the definitive diagnosis?','General Medicine','Infectious Diseases','AI Predicted 2026','upsc-cms'),('cpo-1','Voice and Narration conversions make up 45+ questions in SSC CPO Paper 2.',0,'Easy','Simple past tense active (\"repaired\") converts to simple past passive (\"was/were + past participle\").','[\"My car was repaired flawlessly by the mechanic.\",\"My car is being repaired flawlessly by the mechanic.\",\"My car has been repaired flawlessly by the mechanic.\",\"My car will be repaired flawlessly by the mechanic.\"]','Select the correct passive form of the given sentence: \"The mechanic repaired my car flawlessy.\"','English Grammar & Vocabulary','Active / Passive Voice','2024','ssc-cpo'),('ctet-1','Piaget, Vygotsky and Kohlberg theories account for 20% of all CDP questions across TET examinations.',1,'Easy','The Sensorimotor stage (birth 